  "title": "epan: Check lengths on FT_UINT_BYTES",
  "description": "Ensure that the requested bytes actually exist in the tvb before\ncalling tvb_get_ptr(), allocating a byte array, and copying bytes\ninto that array.\n\nWe could distinguish a little more between a FT_BYTES and FT_UINT_BYTES.\nFor a FT_UINT_BYTES, where the length is obtained from packet data,\nthis is certainly an exception. For some FT_BYTES calls this is perhaps\nbetter classified as a dissector bug.\n\nFix #19048",
